{"at": "2026-10-14T18:39:24Z", "problem": 655, "tier": "scout", "outcome": "complete", "spend": 14.1909, "run_dir": "runs/20261009-225323-779500-erdos655", "validated_new": 3, "significance": [1, 1, 1], "arm": "pass", "settle_screen": 0.875, "claim": "deep/C1", "answer": "false", "statement": "For every c > 0 and every n with n ≥ ⌈2/c⌉+3, the n-gon X_n = {e(ζ^j) : 0 ≤ j < n} (ζ = exp(2πi/n), e: ℂ ≅ ℝ² isometry) satisfies #X_n = n, IsValid X_n, and |{dist p q : p,q ∈ X_n}| ≤ ⌊n/2⌋+1 < (1+c)n/2. Hence ¬erdos_655.", "intent": "formalization-gap", "intent_source": "erdosproblems.com #655 forum discussion (Hunter, Jan 2026); regular-polygon distance count: Altman, Amer. Math. Monthly 1963"}
